  "aliases": [
    "CVE-2026-114608"
  ],
  "summary": "Pylint: Arbitrary code execution via pickle deserialization of the stats cache in PYLINT_HOME",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nSince 2006 / pylint 0.15.2, pylint caches its stats as pickles in `PYLINT_HOME` and reload them on the next run with `pickle.load`. Someone without access to the configuration or linted code, but with access to the cache directory (predictable `PYLINT_HOME` on a multi-user host) can write a crafted pickle that will runs arbitrary code when pylint access its stat cache.\n\n### Patches\n\nFrom pylint 4.0.9, the result cache is now stored as JSON instead of pickle, preventing code-execution. \n\n### Workarounds\n\nUntil upgrading do not point `PYLINT_HOME` to an untrusted, shared, or group-writable directory. The default value, `~/.cache/pylint`, is writable only by the user running pylint.\n\n### Credits\n\n- Reported privately via Tidelift coordinated disclosure (Dan Lenz).",
